<Full title="komizo — Operate your own Compose hosts" description="Prepare hosts, deploy app-scoped Compose stacks, and inspect your applications over SSH. A CLI and local UI for servers you own, with no hosted account."><div class="shell"><header><a class="brand" href="/">komizo<span>_</span></a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="#workflow">Workflow</a><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/komizo#readme">Docs ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/komizo/releases">Releases ↗</a></nav></header><main id="main-content"><section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="label">HOST OPERATIONS / YOUR INFRASTRUCTURE</div><h1>Your box.<br>Your stack.<br><em>Your call.</em></h1><div class="hero-bottom"><p>Prepare and operate your own Compose hosts over SSH. Deploy one application at a time, inspect what’s running, and keep the work on servers you own.</p><div><a class="button" href="https://github.com/nicodes/komizo#readme">Start with the CLI ↗</a><p class="note">No hosted account required.</p></div></div></div>
<section class="console" aria-label="Komizo command reference"><div class="console-bar"><span>COMMAND REFERENCE</span><span>SSH → YOUR HOST</span></div><div class="console-body"><div><span class="prompt">01</span><code>komizo init</code><p>Prepare a host. Requires privileged access.</p></div><div><span class="prompt">02</span><code>komizo list</code><p>Inspect the applications on your host.</p></div><div><span class="prompt">03</span><code>komizo report</code><p>Read the state of your stack.</p></div><div><span class="prompt">04</span><code>komizo logs</code><p>See what your applications are saying.</p></div></div><p class="console-foot">Use <code>--help</code> for each command’s current flags.</p></section>
</section>
<section class="workflow" id="workflow"><div class="section-title"><p class="label">OPERATE THE WHOLE PATH</p><h2>From host prep<br>to the next deploy.</h2></div><div class="workflow-list"><article><b>01 / PREPARE</b><h3>Give the host a foundation.</h3><p>Start with <code>init</code> on a host you administer. Review the documented changes before provisioning an existing server.</p></article><article><b>02 / DEPLOY</b><h3>A Compose stack per app.</h3><p>The supported deployment model is app-scoped Compose. Use the companion GitHub Actions to connect releases to your hosts.</p><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/komizo-actions">Explore the deployment actions ↗</a></article><article><b>03 / OPERATE</b><h3>Keep a view of the running system.</h3><p>Use the terminal for applications, reports and logs. Prefer a browser? The <code>ui</code> command serves the local interface.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="install"><div><p class="label">PICK YOUR ENTRY POINT</p><h2>Small tool.<br>Real infrastructure.</h2><p>Choose a verified release archive or install with a Go toolchain matching the project’s requirements.</p></div><div class="install-options"><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/komizo/releases"><span>01</span><div><b>Prebuilt releases</b><p>Linux and macOS · x86_64 and arm64</p></div><i>↗</i></a><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/komizo#readme"><span>02</span><div><b>Install and command guide</b><p>Host preparation, current commands and release verification</p></div><i>↗</i></a><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/komizo-actions"><span>03</span><div><b>GitHub Actions</b><p>App-scoped Compose deployments from CI</p></div><i>↗</i></a></div></section></main><footer><span>komizo / CLI + LOCAL UI</span><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/komizo">Source on GitHub ↗</a></footer></div></Full>
<style>

